VTID-03786 — commands.log
==========================

## Live-browser attempt (failed — environment limitation, not a code issue)

Attempted a real Playwright/Chromium session against
https://preview-aws.vitanaland.com to visually retest VTID-03785. Every
navigation attempt failed:

  net::ERR_CONNECTION_RESET

Tried, in order, none changed the outcome:
  - explicit `proxy: { server: 'http://127.0.0.1:40877' }` launch option
  - `--proxy-server=http://127.0.0.1:40877` chromium arg
  - `--ignore-certificate-errors` + `ignoreHTTPSErrors: true`
  - `--no-sandbox --disable-setuid-sandbox`
  - `--disable-ipv6`
  - Chromium netlog capture (--log-net-log) confirmed the CONNECT request
    reaches the proxy (`CONNECT preview-aws.vitanaland.com:443 HTTP/1.1`)
    but the connection resets immediately after, with no relay-failure
    entry recorded on the proxy's own /__agentproxy/status endpoint.

Isolated: a raw Node `net`+`tls` socket manually doing the identical
CONNECT tunnel + TLS handshake through the SAME proxy port reaches the
SAME host fine (real 200 response, real page content, cert CN=vitanaland.com)
— ruling out a network-wide block on the host and confirming this is
specific to headless Chromium's own connection in this sandbox.

